WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.418
Hi! Today we'll join two sentences using relative pronouns and participles. These come up a lot in Primary 5 synthesis.

2
00:00:11.568 --> 00:00:19.530
Who is for a person who does the action. The girl won. She is my friend becomes: The girl who won is my friend.

3
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:28.266
Whom is for a person who receives the action. You met the boy. He is my cousin becomes: The boy whom you met is my cousin.

4
00:00:28.416 --> 00:00:36.162
Whose shows possession. I met a man. His dog was lost becomes: I met a man whose dog was lost.

5
00:00:36.312 --> 00:00:40.578
Which is for things and animals: This is the book which I bought.

6
00:00:40.728 --> 00:00:45.690
Where is for places: This is the park where we play.

7
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:58.458
Participles can join sentences too. He finished his homework. He went out to play becomes: Having finished his homework, he went out to play. It shows the homework came first.

8
00:00:58.608 --> 00:01:07.842
She heard the news. She cried becomes: Hearing the news, she cried. Both parts must have the same subject.

9
00:01:07.992 --> 00:01:12.114
Watch out! This is the book which I bought it is wrong!

10
00:01:12.264 --> 00:01:16.674
Which already stands for the book, so writing it again repeats it.

11
00:01:16.824 --> 00:01:23.442
After combining, remember to remove repeated words like it, him or her.

12
00:01:23.592 --> 00:01:34.362
Your turn! The man is a doctor. He lives next door. Join them with who. Pause and think.

13
00:01:34.512 --> 00:01:41.322
The answer is: The man who lives next door is a doctor. Did you get it right?

14
00:01:41.472 --> 00:01:52.290
Another one! I have a friend. Her mother is a pilot. Join them with whose. Pause and think.

15
00:01:52.440 --> 00:02:00.642
The answer is: I have a friend whose mother is a pilot. Whose replaces her. Did you get it right?

16
00:02:00.792 --> 00:02:11.730
Here's another! Mum opened the door. She saw a parcel. Begin with Opening. Pause and think.

17
00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:20.970
The answer is: Opening the door, Mum saw a parcel. Mum is the subject of both parts. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:31.986
One more! This is the hawker centre. We had dinner there. Join them with where. Pause and think.

19
00:02:32.136 --> 00:02:40.818
The answer is: This is the hawker centre where we had dinner. Where replaces there. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:51.666
And another! The cake is delicious. My aunt baked it. Join them with which. Pause and think.

21
00:02:51.816 --> 00:03:00.450
The answer is: The cake which my aunt baked is delicious. Notice it is removed. Did you get it right?

22
00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:13.266
Remember: who and whom for people, whose for possession, which for things, and where for places. With a participle opener, both parts need the same subject. And remove repeated pronouns.

23
00:03:13.416 --> 00:03:17.682
Try introducing a friend using whose!

